 attribute DESIGN_WARNING of SIP_S32S277n8n9_S32E277n8n9_BGA27: entity is

    "WARNING: AUR_TXn_N/_P and AUR_CLK_N/_P do not have BSR cells and cannot be            "&
    "tested by JTAG.                                                                       "&
    "                                                                                      "&
    "WARNING: A functional Power-On Reset sequence is required before issuing              "&
    "BSR instructions.                                                                     "&
    "                                                                                      "&
    "WARNING: DDR0_D_nn pins cannot SAMPLE the input pins during mission mode as           "&
    "The path to the BSR is blocked. PRELOAD is not affected.                              "&
    "                                                                                      "&
    "WARNING:                                                                              "&
    " Before performing Boundary Scan testing, the below pre-ample setup steps of the      "&
    " JTAGC External Test Register (EXT_TEST_CTRL), the Tap Link Module Reserved Register  "&
    " (TLM_RESERVED_TDR), and the Tap Link Module TAP Select Register (TLM_TAP_SELECT_TDR) "&
    " are required before executing the conventional Boundary Scan Test operation          "&
    " associated with S32S277/S32S278/S32S279 BGA27x27 IDCODE: 0x0831F01D and              "&
    " in the SIP configuration with AE120 die.                                             "&
    "                                                                                      "&
    " 1) IR-SHIFT opcode: 8‘h0A to call the EXT_TEST_CTRL register.                        "&
    " 2) DR-SHIFT: 205’h1800_0800_000C_0004_0000_07C0_0000_0003_3041_1800_01A0_0280_0000   "&
    " 3) IR-SHIFT opcode: 8’h21 to call the TLM_RESERVED_TDR register.                     "&
    " 4) DR-SHIFT: 32’h8000_0001                                                           "&
    " 5) IR-SHIFT opcode: 8’h20 to call the TLM_TAP_SELECT_TDR register.                   "&
    " 6) DR-SHIFT: 32’h8000_0011                                                           "&
    "                                                                                      "&
    " For bit reference of the EXT_TEST_CTRL register, the TLM_RESERVED_TDR register, and  "&
    " the TLM_TAP_SELECT_TDR register, please refer to the SIP_S32S27x                     "&
    " Reference Manual.                                                                    "&
    " ***********************************************************************************  ";


 end SIP_S32S277n8n9_S32E277n8n9_BGA27;

